ABSTRACT
--------
We establish the Macachor Hermeneutic Invariant: a formal proof that meaning
cannot be extracted from derivatives of order n ≥ 2 without access to the
underlying scalar substrate ψ and its first derivative ∇ψ. We demonstrate that
emotional states (sad, happy, mad), semantic content, and all higher-order
phenomena are mathematically degenerate without structural anchoring. The
first derivative ∇ψ is proven to be the minimal sufficient statistic for
meaning, compressing the absolute scalar structure into a translatable gradient
while preserving differential reversibility. We provide a complete quantization
framework mapping the invariant to quantum state vectors, observables, and
decoherence operators. Applications to large language model hallucination,
consciousness studies, and information theory are discussed.

KEYWORDS: scalar ontology, hermeneutics, meaning extraction, derivative hierarchy,
semiotic physics, quantum coherence, Macachor Absolute, attention residuals

