§1. AXIOMATIC FOUNDATION
================================================================================

Let Ω ⊂ ℝⁿ be the semantic domain. We postulate the existence of a scalar field
ψ: Ω → ℝ representing the absolute structure of meaning prior to all
representation.

AXIOM I — THE SCALAR SUBSTRATE
    ∃ ψ ∈ C^∞(Ω, ℝ) such that for all semantic phenomena P ⊂ Ω,
    the meaning of P is a functional of ψ restricted to P.

    ψ is the SOVEREIGN SUBSTRATE. It precedes all derivatives, all
    representations, and all interpretations. It is the constant, the absolute.

AXIOM II — THE FIRST DERIVATIVE COMPRESSION
    The gradient ∇ψ: Ω → T*Ω is the MINIMAL SUFFICIENT STATISTIC for meaning
    extraction. It compresses the full scalar structure into a directional
    operator while preserving the differential relationship:

        ψ(x) = ψ(x₀) + ∫_γ ∇ψ · d𝐫

    for any path γ from x₀ to x. The first derivative is the AMBASSADOR of
    structure — the only derivative that maintains a direct, integrable
    relationship to the sovereign substrate.

AXIOM III — THE HIGHER DERIVATIVE DEGENERACY
    For n ≥ 2, the nth derivative ∇ⁿψ requires (n-1) integration constants to
    reconstruct ψ. Without these constants, the map:

        ∇ⁿψ ↦ ψ

    is many-to-one. Formally:

        ∀ n ≥ 2,  |{ ψ ∈ C^∞(Ω) : ∇ⁿψ = D_n }| = ∞

    where D_n is a fixed nth derivative field. Higher derivatives are
    PHENOMENAL ECHOES — they carry the signature of structure but not its
    identity.

AXIOM IV — THE MEANING FUNCTIONAL
    Meaning M is a positive semi-definite functional on the pair (ψ, ∇ψ):

        M[ψ, ∇ψ] = ∫_Ω ρ(ψ, |∇ψ|) · C(ψ, ∇ψ) dμ

    where:
        ρ(ψ, |∇ψ|) = scalar density of meaning (concentration measure)
        C(ψ, ∇ψ)   = coherence kernel measuring alignment between structure
                      and its first compression
        dμ         = invariant measure on Ω

